#+TITLE: alfe suite fails on a Mac with a licensed, runnable AutoCAD
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: test
#+DEPENDS:
#+BRANCH: fix-alfe-tests-on-macos-with-autocad
#+DATE: 2026-11-13

* Symptom
=make -C autolisp-front-end test-sbcl= on release-2.4.0, on thalassa (macOS,
AutoCAD 2027 installed and licensed): 3 failures out of 2700 checks.

- =ACCORECONSOLE-MACOS-IS-OPT-IN-NOT-AUTO-DISCOVERED=:
  =(discover-accoreconsole-binary :os :macos)= returned the real
  =/Applications/Autodesk/AutoCAD 2027/.../AcCoreConsole= instead of NIL.
- =CONFORMANCE-CORPUS-PASSES=: =autocad-unsupported-os: stderr missing
  substring "not distributed"=.
- =AUTOCAD-DETECT-ON-MACOS-REQUIRES-A-RUNNABLE-ACCORECONSOLE=: the discovered
  path was =/private/var/folders/...=, the expected one =/var/folders/...=.

* Cause
All three come from alfe 2.3.118 (2026-11-09), "macOS AutoCAD available only
once its AcCoreConsole runs": an AcCoreConsole found in a macOS AutoCAD bundle
is now discovered once a probe has seen it run AutoLISP. The CI macOS runners
have no runnable AutoCAD, so nothing showed there; this Mac has one.

1. The opt-in guard (alfe 1.7.13, 2026-08-02) asserted the superseded rule
   "never auto-discovered" and read the host's real =/Applications=.
2. The conformance runner built its AutoCAD-absent baseline by unsetting
   =$AUTOCAD_ACCORECONSOLE= only; with bundle discovery, the real install was
   found, so =--autocad= was available and =autocad-unsupported-os= failed. Its
   first run also paid the real 120 s runnability probe.
3. =%fake-accoreconsole= returned the path under =(uiop:temporary-directory)=
   (=/var/folders=, a symlink on macOS), while =DIRECTORY= returns truenames
   (=/private/var/folders=). The =(search exe message)= assertion in the same
   test only passed because one is a substring of the other.

* Resolved (clautolisp 2.4.2 / alfe 2.4.2)
- =alfe.conformance::call-without-installed-autocad=: =RUN-SCENARIO= points the
  macOS bundle search at an empty place under the scenario's workdir, except
  for =:autocad-only= scenarios, which mean to drive the real AutoCAD.
  Scenario description and the sandbox comment updated.
- Guard rewritten and renamed =ACCORECONSOLE-MACOS-DISCOVERED-ONLY-WHEN-RUNNABLE=,
  on a fake =/Applications=: no bundle -> NIL; unrunnable bundle -> NIL;
  =$AUTOCAD_ACCORECONSOLE= taken as given, unprobed.
- New =CONFORMANCE-RUNS-AGAINST-AN-AUTOCAD-ABSENT-BASELINE=: runs
  =autocad-unsupported-os= with a fake runnable install bound; fails without
  the runner change (reproduces the 2.4.0 failure), passes with it, on every
  POSIX host.
- =%fake-accoreconsole= returns the truename.
